                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "My office has received several calls and e-mails regarding cuts at the Department of Veterans Affairs that I\u2019d like to address.\n\nI recently met with the Director of the North Florida/South Georgia VA Healthcare System, who shared that only 20 of their 6,600 employees (or 0.3%) were laid off. All of them were recent hires, and NONE of them were direct patient care positions.\n\nMy team has also spoken with the Director of the Gulf Coast VA Healthcare System, who shared that they have lost a \u201cminimal\u201d number of employees, and none of them were direct patient care positions. In fact, they\u2019ve received multiple waivers and continue to hire direct patient care positions.\n\nAs a veteran, ensuring my fellow veterans receive the medical care they\u2019ve earned and support during the claims process they deserve is a top priority. That is why I was proud to vote for the recent budget resolution that increased VA funding for Fiscal Year 2025. If you\u2019re a veteran who needs help, please call my Panama City District Office at (850) 785-0812 or visit my website at https://t.co/Ixl3uA8iF5 to request assistance.",
